    "narrative": "The Austin Waves\u2019 lineup today is headlined by **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (84.88) and **Gunnar Henderson** (83.29), our premier offensive anchors. **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** benefits from a favorable matchup against a high-ERA arm in Lodolo, where the combination of favorable park factors and dynamic platoon splits against the left-hander elevates his floor. Similarly, **Gunnar Henderson** finds himself in a \"smash\" spot against Beck; the high xERA of the opposing starter, paired with an elite order position and dynamic platoon advantages, creates massive upside for run production. While **Kyle Tucker** (80.19) trails slightly in the raw metrics, his outlook is buoyed by a strong wind-out factor and a soft matchup against Marte, solidifying the top of our card as the core engine for today\u2019s 5x5 push.\n\nThe most challenging bench decision centered on **Luis Lara** (51.52), who narrowly missed the cut for the final outfield slot. While **Luis Lara** provided a respectable score, the optimizer favored **Andy Pages** (65.80) due to a superior matchup against Marte and favorable wind conditions that offset **Andy Pages**' lower batting order position. We are also keeping a watchful eye on our \"Lineup Pending\" status for **Jackson Merrill**, **Henry Bolte**, **Kyle Tucker**, and **Andy Pages**; while these projections assume specific order placements, any late-breaking shifts could necessitate a recalibration to ensure we aren\u2019t sacrificing plate appearances. Additionally, while **Heliot Ramos** (57.74) offers sneaky stolen base potential against Rogers, his score is tempered by a tougher opposing pitcher, making him a marginal play compared to the high-efficiency ceiling of our primary starters.",
